    4. For each H segment, pick column span (length 4-18) within grid bounds.
    5. For each V segment, pick row span (length 4-18) within grid bounds.
    6. Verify at least 1 H-V crossing exists; if not, adjust spans to create one.
    7. Verify no H-H overlap on any row and no V-V overlap on any column.
    8. Build output by drawing H segments first, then V segments (V wins at crossings).
    9. Derive input by keeping only the two endpoint pixels of each segment.
